    <section class="flowchart-section">
        <div class="flowchart-container">
            <div class="flowchart">
                <div class="step">
                    <div class="step-number">STEP 1</div>
                    <div class="step-title">Analyze the Stimulus</div>
                    <div class="step-content">
                        <ul>
                            <li>Combine premises</li>
                            <li>Ask: What would I conclude?</li>
                            <li>Compare to author's conclusion</li>
                            <li>Try to state exact flaw</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="arrow">↓</div>
                
                <div class="step highlight">
                    <div class="step-number">STEP 2</div>
                    <div class="step-title">Prediction Check</div>
                    <div class="step-content">
                        <ul>
                            <li>Predict: What is the flaw?</li>
                            <li>If you have a prediction → Hunt Mode (scan for it)</li>
                            <li>If no prediction or scan doesn't land → Start with A</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="arrow">↓</div>
                
                <div class="step">
                    <div class="step-number">STEP 3</div>
                    <div class="step-title">Recognize Answer Choice Type</div>
                    <div class="step-content">
                        Three common forms:
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="arrow">↓</div>
                
                <div class="branch-container">
                    <div class="branch">
                        <div class="step-title">Descriptive Answers</div>
                        <div class="step-content">
                            Often starts "the argument concludes..."
                            <ul>
                                <li>Check descriptive accuracy</li>
                                <li>If accurate, ask: Is this a flaw?</li>
                                <li>Yes = Correct</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="branch">
                        <div class="step-title">Assumption-Based Answers</div>
                        <div class="step-content">
                            Often starts "the argument presumes..."
                            <ul>
                                <li>Apply NA Test</li>
                                <li>MBT: Would this need to be true?</li>
                                <li>Negation: If false, does argument collapse?</li>
                                <li>Yes = Correct</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="branch">
                        <div class="step-title">Fails to Consider / Ignores</div>
                        <div class="step-content">
                            Often 5-star Flaw questions
                            <ul>
                                <li>Apply Weaken Test</li>
                                <li>Take answer as true (new premise)</li>
                                <li>Does it weaken the argument?</li>
                                <li>Yes = Correct</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="arrow">↓</div>
                
                <div class="step final-step">
                    <div class="step-title">Correct Answer Check</div>
                    <div class="step-content">
                        Accurately describes a real weakness in the argument's reasoning
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

